	"transcription": [
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:00,000",
				"to": "00:00:04,820"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 0,
				"to": 4820
			},
			"text": " This is a question from Alex, who asks, \"What if a Richter Magnitude 15 earthquake were"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:04,820",
				"to": "00:00:07,340"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 4820,
				"to": 7340
			},
			"text": " to hit America at, let's say, New York City?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:07,340",
				"to": "00:00:09,580"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 7340,
				"to": 9580
			},
			"text": " What about a Richter Zero, or 25?\""
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:09,580",
				"to": "00:00:13,820"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 9580,
				"to": 13820
			},
			"text": " Well, given that a magnitude 25 quake would destroy the sun if one happened there, it"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:13,820",
				"to": "00:00:19,100"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 13820,
				"to": 19100
			},
			"text": " would certainly destroy New York City, but we're getting ahead of ourselves."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:19,100",
				"to": "00:00:22,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 19100,
				"to": 22720
			},
			"text": " The Richter scale, which has technically been replaced by the Moment Magnitude scale, measures"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:22,720",
				"to": "00:00:24,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 22720,
				"to": 24320
			},
			"text": " the strength of an earthquake."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:24,320",
				"to": "00:00:27,820"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 24320,
				"to": 27820
			},
			"text": " Since we usually hear about earthquakes with ratings somewhere between 3 and 9, a lot of"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:27,820",
				"to": "00:00:31,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 27820,
				"to": 31240
			},
			"text": " people probably think of 10 as the top of the scale and 0 as the bottom."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:31,240",
				"to": "00:00:34,060"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 31240,
				"to": 34060
			},
			"text": " In fact, there is no top or bottom to the scale."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:34,060",
				"to": "00:00:36,920"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 34060,
				"to": 36920
			},
			"text": " But even if 10 isn't the top of the scale, it might as well be."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:36,920",
				"to": "00:00:40,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 36920,
				"to": 40520
			},
			"text": " A magnitude 9 earthquake already measurably alters the rotation of the earth."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:40,520",
				"to": "00:00:44,500"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 40520,
				"to": 44500
			},
			"text": " The two magnitude 9+ earthquakes this century both altered the length of the day by a tiny"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:44,500",
				"to": "00:00:46,440"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 44500,
				"to": 46440
			},
			"text": " but measurable fraction of a second."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:46,440",
				"to": "00:00:50,000"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 46440,
				"to": 50000
			},
			"text": " In order to get to magnitude 10, you'd need a ruptured fault line 3 and a half thousand"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:50,000",
				"to": "00:00:53,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 50000,
				"to": 53960
			},
			"text": " kilometers long, and a magnitude 11 quake would require a fault that went halfway around"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:53,960",
				"to": "00:00:54,960"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 53960,
				"to": 54960
			},
			"text": " the world."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:54,960",
				"to": "00:00:58,800"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 54960,
				"to": 58800
			},
			"text": " A magnitude 15 earthquake would be a million times more powerful than that, and involve"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:00:58,800",
				"to": "00:01:02,460"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 58800,
				"to": 62460
			},
			"text": " the release of enough energy to evaporate all the water on earth, though if that happened"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:02,460",
				"to": "00:01:05,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 62460,
				"to": 65760
			},
			"text": " we could rest easy knowing the earthquake couldn't cause any tsunamis."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:05,760",
				"to": "00:01:10,180"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 65760,
				"to": 70180
			},
			"text": " Going a few steps further, a magnitude 18 earthquake would release nearly 10^32 joules"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:10,180",
				"to": "00:01:13,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 70180,
				"to": 73680
			},
			"text": " of energy, which is roughly the gravitational binding energy of the earth."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:13,680",
				"to": "00:01:17,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 73680,
				"to": 77840
			},
			"text": " To put it another way, the Death Star caused a magnitude 18 earthquake on Alderaan."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:17,840",
				"to": "00:01:21,380"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 77840,
				"to": 81380
			},
			"text": " You could in theory talk about a more powerful earthquake on Earth, but in practice all it"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:21,380",
				"to": "00:01:25,200"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 81380,
				"to": 85200
			},
			"text": " would mean is that the expanding cloud of space debris would be faster and hotter."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:25,200",
				"to": "00:01:29,560"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 85200,
				"to": 89560
			},
			"text": " The Sun, with its higher gravitational binding energy, could have up to a magnitude 24 quake."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:29,560",
				"to": "00:01:32,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 89560,
				"to": 92880
			},
			"text": " This is about the energy release you would get if you packed the entire volume of Jupiter"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:32,880",
				"to": "00:01:35,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 92880,
				"to": 95520
			},
			"text": " with hydrogen bombs and detonated them all at once."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:35,520",
				"to": "00:01:39,080"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 95520,
				"to": 99080
			},
			"text": " The most powerful quakes in the known universe, which occur in super heavy neutron stars,"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:39,080",
				"to": "00:01:40,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 99080,
				"to": 100400
			},
			"text": " are about this magnitude."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:40,400",
				"to": "00:01:43,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 100400,
				"to": 103160
			},
			"text": " A magnitude 25 quake would explode the Sun."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:43,160",
				"to": "00:01:47,320"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 103160,
				"to": 107320
			},
			"text": " Hold on, we're spending a lot of time thinking about things that are large and violent."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:47,320",
				"to": "00:01:48,560"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 107320,
				"to": 108560
			},
			"text": " What about the bottom end of the scale?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:48,560",
				"to": "00:01:51,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 108560,
				"to": 111360
			},
			"text": " Is there such a thing as a magnitude 0 earthquake?"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:51,360",
				"to": "00:01:54,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 111360,
				"to": 114400
			},
			"text": " Yes, in fact the scale goes all the way down past zero."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:54,400",
				"to": "00:01:57,880"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 114400,
				"to": 117880
			},
			"text": " Let's take a look at some low magnitude earthquakes with a description of what they would be like"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:57,880",
				"to": "00:01:59,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 117880,
				"to": 119240
			},
			"text": " if they hit your house."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:01:59,240",
				"to": "00:02:03,400"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 119240,
				"to": 123400
			},
			"text": " A magnitude 1 quake releases the same energy as dropping a partially loaded cement truck"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:03,400",
				"to": "00:02:06,080"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 123400,
				"to": 126080
			},
			"text": " from 10 meters onto the street in front of your house."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:06,080",
				"to": "00:02:09,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 126080,
				"to": 129720
			},
			"text": " A magnitude 0 earthquake is equivalent to the Dallas Cowboys American football team"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:09,720",
				"to": "00:02:12,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 129720,
				"to": 132720
			},
			"text": " running it full tilled into the side of your neighbor's garage."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:12,720",
				"to": "00:02:16,640"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 132720,
				"to": 136640
			},
			"text": " A magnitude negative 1 quake is like a single American football player running into a tree"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:16,640",
				"to": "00:02:17,720"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 136640,
				"to": 137720
			},
			"text": " in your yard."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:17,720",
				"to": "00:02:21,160"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 137720,
				"to": 141160
			},
			"text": " A cat falling off a dresser would have a magnitude of negative 2."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:21,160",
				"to": "00:02:24,840"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 141160,
				"to": 144840
			},
			"text": " A cat knocking your cell phone off your nightstand would have a magnitude negative 3."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:24,840",
				"to": "00:02:28,080"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 144840,
				"to": 148080
			},
			"text": " Magnitude negative 4 is like a penny falling off of a dog."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:28,080",
				"to": "00:02:32,480"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 148080,
				"to": 152480
			},
			"text": " Magnitude negative 5 is a key press on an IBM Model M mechanical keyboard."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:32,480",
				"to": "00:02:35,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 152480,
				"to": 155360
			},
			"text": " Negative 6 is a key press on a lightweight keyboard."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:35,360",
				"to": "00:02:38,520"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 155360,
				"to": 158520
			},
			"text": " Negative 7 is a single feather fluttering to the ground."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:38,520",
				"to": "00:02:42,240"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 158520,
				"to": 162240
			},
			"text": " A fine grain of sand falling onto the pile at the bottom of a tiny hourglass would be"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:42,240",
				"to": "00:02:44,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 162240,
				"to": 164360
			},
			"text": " a magnitude negative 8 quake."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:44,360",
				"to": "00:02:48,760"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 164360,
				"to": 168760
			},
			"text": " And let's jump all the way down to magnitude negative 15, a drifting mode of dust coming"
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:48,760",
				"to": "00:02:50,680"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 168760,
				"to": 170680
			},
			"text": " to rest gently on a table."
		},
		{
			"timestamps": {
				"from": "00:02:50,680",
				"to": "00:02:53,360"
			},
			"offsets": {
				"from": 170680,
				"to": 173360
			},
			"text": " Sometimes it's nice not to destroy the world for a change."
		}
	]
}
